// Excingos the smith. Sells arms.
=== start
He doesn't stop hammering. "Spears, the king's. Swords, the nobles'. Anything left over is for sale." The hammer comes down. "Not much left over."
* "Let's trade." -> trade
* "Busy?" -> busy
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== trade
~ barter
"Pay in silver. I've been paid in promises all winter."
* "Thanks." -> start

=== busy
"Six hundred spearheads by the new moon." He wipes his face and leaves a black stripe. "My apprentice went for a soldier. My wife does the bellows. The king's man comes every evening to count." He laughs. "I've never been so rich or so tired."
* "Goodbye." -> END
